# Line-ending normalization. Without this, git prints
# "warning: in the working copy of '...', LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every
# diff/add over the memory-bank record files, and those warnings push the
# "N files changed" line out of the readable part of the output
# (memory-bank/gotchas/git.md, measured 13 Nov 2026). eol=crlf also makes the
# record diffs stable, which is why they can be committed at all.
*.md text eol=crlf
